brief:
The person tagged the bot in a reply. The post they tagged it in says:
@buildthis.bisks.net a Google Drive clone that stores it's files encrypted in an ATProto PDS. Make it run entirely in a browser. Use the File System API to let the user select files. Use Web Crypto to encrypt files. Split them into 50MB chunks, and then post them to the user's PDS.

The thread it's replying to, oldest first (this is the context "this" refers to):
@jessehattabaugh.com: Where do you think the Bluesky limits actually are?

What if I follow everybody, like every post, repost every other post, etc.?

What if I create an oauth app and start posting tons of copyrighted data into some new lexicon.

When does bsky cut you off, and say "no more PDS for you"
@jessehattabaugh.com: The dev guidelines make a distinction between automated and manual actions, but there's no publicly documented universal per-account storage quota for arbitrary custom records.
@jessehattabaugh.com: Hey @attie.ai can you build me a Google Drive clone that stores it's files encrypted in an ATProto PDS? 😈
@jessehattabaugh.com: This is joke @attie.ai I know you can't do oauth
